%description:

TcpCubic.delta:invalid -- a negative time stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts 0 and more.

The classes: settling (10ms, the default) and long (a time longer than the run), invalid
(below 0). The code: the RTT samples of the first delta of an epoch are ignored
(TcpCubic::processRttSample()); the smallest sample is cubic_delay_min.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.delta
%# class: invalid
%# value: -1s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.delta
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicDeltaInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.delta = -1s    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
delta must be 0 or more, but it is -1s
